    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 19:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.19.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.19.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 19:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“But I know everything about you, what you do and where you go. I know how you rage against me. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.19.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.19.27"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "28",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 19:28"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "28",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I have received the report of that rage and that pride of yours, and now I will put a hook through your nose and a bit in your mouth, and take you back by the same road you came.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.19.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.19.28"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "28",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 19:28"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "28",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.19.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.19.28"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "29",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 19:29"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "29",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Isaiah said to King Hezekiah, “This is a sign of what will happen. This year and next you will have only wild grain to eat, but the following year you will be able to sow your corn and harvest it, and plant vines and eat grapes. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.19.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.19.29"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "30",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 19:30"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "30",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Those in Judah who survive will flourish like plants that send roots deep into the ground and produce fruit. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.19.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.19.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "31",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 19:31"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "31",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "There will be people in Jerusalem and on Mount Zion who will survive, because the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.19.31",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.19.31"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " is determined to make this happen.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.19.31",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.19.31"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "31",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 19:31"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "31",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.19.31",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.19.31"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "32",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 19:32"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "32",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“This is what the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.19.32",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.19.32"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " has said about the Assyrian emperor: ‘He will not enter this city or shoot a single arrow against it. No soldiers with shields will come near the city, and no siege mounds will be built round it. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.19.32",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.19.32"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "33",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 19:33"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "33",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He will go back by the same road he came, without entering this city. I, the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.19.33",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.19.33"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", have spoken. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.19.33",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.19.33"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "34",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 19:34"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "34",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I will defend this city and protect it, for the sake of my own honour and because of the promise I made to my servant David.’ ”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.19.34",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.19.34"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "34",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 19:34"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "34",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.19.34",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.19.34"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "35",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 19:35"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "35",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "That night an angel of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.19.35",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.19.35"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " went to the Assyrian camp and killed 185,000 soldiers. At dawn the next day, there they lay, all dead! ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.19.35",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.19.35"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "36",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 19:36"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "36",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then the Assyrian emperor Sennacherib withdrew and returned to Nineveh. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.19.36",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.19.36"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "37",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 19:37"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "37",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "One day, when he was worshipping in the temple of his god Nisroch, two of his sons, Adrammelech and Sharezer, killed him with their swords, and then escaped to the land of Ararat. Another of his sons, Esarhaddon, succeeded him as emperor.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.19.37",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.19.37"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
